      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Bank deposits are the first tool most people use to save. They are safe, simple, and insured in most countries. But not all deposits are the same, and choosing the wrong one can cost you thousands. Types of Bank Deposits Type How It Works Access Typical Rate Best For Checking Account No restrictions, instant access Anytime 0-1% Daily spending Savings Account Some limits on withdrawals 24-48 hours 1-4% Short-term savings Fixed-Term Deposit\tLocked for set period (3-24 months)At maturity 4-12% Medium-term goals High-Yield Deposit Higher rate, longer lock-up At maturity 8-16% Long-term saving What to Compare Before Opening a Deposit 4 Annual Interest Rate (APY) The actual return after compounding. Always compare APY, not the headline rate. A 12% rate compounded monthly is actually 12.68% APY. 4 Compounding Frequency Monthly compounding beats annual compounding. Money makes money faster when interest is calculated more often. 4 Minimum Balance Some high-yield accounts require $1,000+ minimum. Make sure you can meet it without touching emergency funds. 4 Early Withdrawal Penalty If you break a fixed deposit early, you may lose ALL interest earned. Know the penalty before you commit. 4 Deposit Insurance Is your money insured by the government? Up to what amount? In most countries, deposits up to $100,000-250,000 are protected."
